(version 1)

# No project-local design-rule exceptions are currently needed.
#
# This file previously carried a "U5 local via size exception" that allowed
# 0.45mm/0.20mm vias inside U5's (BME680, LGA-8, 0.8mm pitch) courtyard,
# because on the old 2-layer layout the +3V3 pin could only be reached by a
# via that did not fit at board-standard 0.6mm.
#
# That exception is obsolete since the board moved to a 4-layer stackup:
# +3V3 is now a solid inner plane (In2.Cu), so U5's power pins are bonded
# straight down to it with ordinary 0.6mm/0.3mm vias placed off-pad next to
# the part. Every via on the board is now 0.6mm/0.3mm, i.e. at or above the
# board-wide minimum, so no exception applies.
#
# Keep the file: `kicad-cli` picks up `.kicad_dru` by path, so running the
# checks against the project directory (rather than a detached copy of
# `.kicad_pcb`) stays the correct habit if a rule is ever added back.
